<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">France</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as French</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">France is a country in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> that grew from the western part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>. It built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a> overseas and was a central actor in European power politics, appearing in the histories of empires from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>. French colonial expansion also ended the independence of Sahelian states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/france.jpg" alt="France" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown Vector: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_France.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
